// Protocols for conversations that can be rolled back, from "Compliance for
// reversible client/server interactions" (Barbanera, Dezani-Ciancaglini and
// de'Liguoro).
//
// A behaviour says what one party does. `offer { a: b, ... }` waits for the
// other party to pick an action, `select { a: b, ... }` picks one, `end` is
// success and `rec x { ... }` repeats. A `checkpoint` marks a point that both
// parties can roll the conversation back to. A session with one role declares
// the client and takes the server to be its dual; with two roles the first is
// the client and the second the server. The compiler checks that the client
// is checkpoint compliant with the server: whatever either does, including
// rolling back to its last checkpoint, they never get stuck. Lean checks the
// same independently (`roop lean`).

// The travel agency of the paper. The client wants a house, or a bungalow at
// sea, or a house in the mountains. Importing it checks the pair.
pub session Booking {
    client: offer {
        sea: offer { house: end, bung: end },
        mount: offer { house: end },
    };
}

// The same agency, where the server may change its mind: after offering a
// house it can roll back to its checkpoint and offer a bungalow instead. For
// the client to survive that, it needs the matching checkpoint: the dual is
// exactly that.
pub session Negotiation {
    client: checkpoint select {
        sea: checkpoint select { house: end, bung: end },
        mount: select { house: end },
    };
}

// A client asks for a house with a garden. The server checkpoints in the
// middle of the conversation and the client does not, which is fine because
// rolling back still lands both in compliant states.
pub session Garden {
    client: checkpoint offer {
        sea: offer { house: offer { garden: end } },
        house: offer { garden: end },
    };
    server: checkpoint select {
        sea: checkpoint select { house: select { garden: end } },
        house: select { garden: end },
    };
}

// Say hello until the server acknowledges.
pub session Handshake {
    client: rec again { select { hello: offer { ack: end, nack: again } } };
}

// A stream of items closed by `done`.
pub session Stream {
    client: rec more { select { item: more, done: end } };
}

// Two-phase commit, from the coordinator's side. The coordinator checkpoints
// before it asks, so a refusal can roll the whole round back.
pub session TwoPhase {
    coordinator: checkpoint select {
        prepare: offer {
            yes: select { commit: end },
            no: select { abort: end },
        },
    };
}

// A request that may be answered, refused or deferred, any number of times.
pub session Request {
    client: rec ask {
        checkpoint select {
            request: offer { reply: end, refused: end, busy: ask },
        }
    };
}
